WolfSSL has many build options.
It is therefore not possible for the repo to be released by its authors as includes + libs, but only as source.
At the same time, we do not want to build WolfSSL within our build.
Nor do we want to download the entire repo before or during our build.
Therefore, we simply pre-build with our desired options and release headers + libs to a .tgz file.
We can the use cmake FetchContent, specifying the .tgz in the URL argument to use the release.

If there are other build options or other versions required elsewhere within the organisation, then
this can be facilitated using the same steps below but with a different branch name.


Steps used to pre-build release to a tgz file
---------------------------------------------

Install packages required to build

apt install autoconf
apt install automake
apt install libtool

Create branch from the tag for building 5.8.2
Note that tag for the release needs to be found on master

git branch 5.8.2_build decea12e223869c8f8f3ab5a53dc90b69f436eb2
git push origin -u 5.8.2_build
git checkout 5.8.2_build

Build and Install

autogen.sh
configure --enable-static --disable-shared --enable-singlethreaded --enable-opensslextra --enable-tlsv12 --enable-tls13 --disable-examples --disable-crypttests --enable-staticmemory
make
make install
mkdir lib
cp /usr/local/lib/libwolfssl.* ./lib
mkdir include
cp -r  /usr/local/include/wolfssl/* ./include
tar czvf 5.8.2_release.tgz ./include ./lib
mkdir release
mv 5.8.2_release.tgz ./release

add, commit and push the lib and include directories

